# The partition's retired floor is checked on every stamped append, as revision 4
# specified. The floor is one value per partition but epochs are per leaf, so
# another leaf's retirement rejects an append the live leaf's own entry admits,
# superseding a leaf that nothing superseded (#5635).
MODULE: CurrentNeverFencedFloorAtAppend
TARGET: CurrentNeverFenced
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the shard checks the partition's retired floor on every stamped append
PERTURBS: OwnAlloc, FloorReject
BOUNDS: WithOtherRetire = TRUE, WithBatch = FALSE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
AppendAdmits(a) == epoch[a] >= memFence
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the partition's retired floor is checked on the append path too.
AppendAdmits(a) == epoch[a] >= memFence /\ epoch[a] > retired
--- END